  "worked_solution": "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=40-20+10=30.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-(-3)}\\cdot (30) \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
